To fix the issue, you can add 
@ParameterObject
 which is adjacent to 
@PageableDefault
 in the binding method


Here are the information of 
@ParameterObject
 and 
@PageableDefault


@ParameterObject
: This annotation (from 
org.springdoc.api.annotations
) tells Springdoc to treat 
Pageable
 as a single object with query parameters (
page, size, sort
) and ensures proper rendering in Swagger UI.


@PageableDefault
: Specifies default values (e.g., 
page = 0, size = 100
). These defaults should now be reflected in Swagger UI.


Here is the code shown below


