I had thought that since the JInternalFrame’s border is 
java.awt.Insets[top=3,left=5,bottom=6,right=6]
, which obviously does not properly account for its title bar height, that it must be responsible for this problem.  That is not the actual cause.


The problem is that, at least on my system, a JComboBox created in the Gnome look-and-feel has an initial height of 35, but only after it is added to a displayable container does its “real” height of 41 get applied.  Basically, the JInternalFrame’s 
pack()
 method doesn’t have access to the real sizes yet.


This is almost certainly a bug.  The workaround is to call 
pack()
 again, once the JComboBoxes have their true sizes.  This can be done in the JInternalFrame’s 
addNotify()
 method:


@Override
public void addNotify() {
    super.addNotify();
    pack();
}



But it is not necessary to subclass JInternalFrame at all.  The same effect can be accomplished with a 
HierarchyListener
:


addHierarchyListener(e -> {
    long flags = e.getChangeFlags();
    if ((flags & HierarchyEvent.DISPLAYABILITY_CHANGED) != 0 &&
        e.getComponent().isDisplayable()) {

        EventQueue.invokeLater(() -> pack());
    }
});





(Everything from here on down is 
incorrect.
  I am leaving it as evidence of a dead end in my research.)


It appears the JInternalFrame’s border is 
java.awt.Insets[top=3,left=5,bottom=6,right=6]
, which obviously does not properly account for its title bar height.  This, in turn, causes 
pack()
 to produce an incorrect preferred size.  I suspect the left and right insets are also off.  This certainly appears to be a bug.


One workaround is to override 
addNotify()
, which is called when a component is made displayable (meaning, the component is in a window and that window has been allocated screen real estate by the system, even though it may not be visible yet).  Since the JInternalFrame is guaranteed to be fully constructed at that point, you can search for its 
BasicInternalFrameTitlePane
 child and use that title bar’s height to compute the proper size:


private static <C extends Component> C findDescendantOfType(
                                            Class<C> type,
                                            Component root) {
    if (type.isInstance(root)) {
        return type.cast(root);
    }

    if (root instanceof Container parent) {
        for (Component child : parent.getComponents()) {
            C match = findDescendantOfType(type, child);
            if (match != null) {
                return match;
            }
        }
    }

    return null;
}

@Override
public void addNotify() {
    super.addNotify();

    Component titleBar =
        findDescendantOfType(BasicInternalFrameTitlePane.class, this);
    if (titleBar != null) {
        titleBar.validate();

        EventQueue.invokeLater(() -> {
            Insets border = getInsets();
            int newWidth = getWidth() + border.left + border.right + 2;
            int newHeight = getHeight()
                - border.top + titleBar.getHeight() + border.bottom;
            setSize(newWidth, newHeight);
        });
    }
}



