The problem is losing thread-locals when switching to a Reactor context. Whenever you call 
.stream()
, this will be executed by Reactor. Reactor has its own way of propagating information, the Context API.


But the Spring AI Tool API is blocking, and therefore does not have access to the Context API. So you need to jump through a few hoops to get this to work.


Assumptions on the project




Using Spring MVC, with 
org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-web


Using MCP sync clients 
spring.ai.mcp.client.type=SYNC


